      <text:p text:style-name="P6105">4. Mandatory Pre-Boarding Preventive Medical Examination</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P6109">As a prerequisite for participating in the educational cruise instruction program and onboard recreational/physical activities, the minor must undergo a comprehensive preventive medical screening. I hereby consent to qualified medical personnel conducting the following evaluation prior to departure: </text:p>
      <text:list text:style-name="L178">
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P6110">General physical examination, vital signs, and cardiovascular screening. </text:p>
       </text:list-item>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P6111">Assessment of physical fitness for travel, educational activities, and moderate sports/recreational waivers. </text:p>
       </text:list-item>
       <text:list-item>
        <text:p text:style-name="P6111">Review of medical history, allergies, and current medications. </text:p>
       </text:list-item>
      </text:list>
      <text:p text:style-name="P6105">5. Travel Authorization &amp; Emergency Medical Consent</text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P6109">I (we) authorize the above-named minor to participate in the educational cruise under the supervision of the designated adult chaperone. In addition, I (we) grant full authority to the chaperone and onboard medical staff to consent to any emergency or routine medical treatment deemed necessary by a licensed physician during the voyage. </text:p>
      <text:p text:style-name="P6105">6. Authorization &amp; Signatures</text:p>
      <table:table table:name="Table15" table:style-name="Table15">
       <table:table-column table:style-name="Table15.A"/>
